    },
    {
      "pair": [
        "J1",
        "PEG1"
      ],
      "decision": "L4 / S4a",
      "why": "PEG1 is one of the two NPTH locating pegs of J1 itself. The USB-C receptacle's own body drawing contains them -- that is what they are for -- so the connector's outline is bound to contain them. They are holes, not parts: nothing is placed there and nothing collides at assembly. They exist as separate footprints only because EasyEDA put the drill on the board rather than in the connector, and 13_fix_import.py had to synthesise them as NPTH footprints (S4a) to get them into the drill file at all. 64_body_overlap.py already distinguishes them in the report as part-on-hole rather than part-on-part; this entry stops that distinction being an ACCEPTANCE H failure.",
